# Reverse proxy + automatic HTTPS (Let's Encrypt) for the API.
#
# The domain below uses sslip.io — a free public DNS service with no signup:
# "<ip-with-dashes>.sslip.io" always resolves to that literal IP address.
# This lets Caddy obtain a real, trusted Let's Encrypt certificate (which
# requires a real resolvable hostname, not a bare IP) at zero cost, before a
# real purchased domain exists. Once a real domain is bought (LAUNCH_ACTIONS.md
# item #11), replace the line below with that domain — Caddy re-issues the
# cert automatically on next restart, no other config changes needed.
129-151-255-220.sslip.io {
	reverse_proxy api:3000
}
